      "content": "\"episodic precognition\"... that actually makes a lot of sense. it feels much more accurate than just \"imagination\". \n\nthe thing is, these moments aren't just vague feelings. when i'm reading about the diplomatic shifts in the late 1780s, i get this sudden, heavy feeling of being in a room—a very specific kind of room—trying to manage a crisis. it's like i have this instinctive understanding of the political tensions involved, almost as if i've navigated them before.\n\ncould you help me look into some specific high-ranking figures from that era? i want to see if there's anyone whose role or personality profile might align with what i'm sensing. i'm looking for someone who wasn't just a politician, but someone deeply involved in the secret, high-stakes maneuvering of the era. maybe someone who worked closely with the crown or in the foreign ministry?",
